WEBVTT

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.728 --> 00:00:04.910
If you work in this trade long enough, sooner or later you will meet it:

00:00:05.011 --> 00:00:08.924
a cut that bleeds, a drop of chemical splashing into an eye,

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.950
or a client who suddenly turns pale and faints.

00:00:12.283 --> 00:00:15.070
In that moment, nobody has time to open a book.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.630
So today, we rehearse it in our heads:

00:00:17.928 --> 00:00:19.790
what do I do in the first minute.

00:00:20.196 --> 00:00:21.390
Let me say this first:

00:00:21.739 --> 00:00:24.510
this lesson does not replace a first aid course.

00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:27.550
Every salon should have someone trained in first aid.

00:00:28.211 --> 00:00:30.847
In every incident, three things are the same.

00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:32.127
Stop working.

00:00:32.401 --> 00:00:36.367
Stay calm, because the client looks at your face to know whether to be scared.

00:00:36.796 --> 00:00:40.207
And if you see danger to life, call emergency services first.

00:00:40.664 --> 00:00:44.607
In the European Union, that number is 112.

00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:46.605
The most common incident:

00:00:46.952 --> 00:00:49.645
you accidentally cut the skin, and it bleeds.

00:00:49.978 --> 00:00:51.965
Stop, and put on new gloves.

00:00:52.299 --> 00:00:55.115
Take clean gauze, press it directly on the cut,

00:00:55.065 --> 00:00:57.645
and hold it still until the bleeding stops.

00:00:58.074 --> 00:01:02.125
Then rinse the wound with clean water, pat it dry, and cover it.

00:01:02.554 --> 00:01:05.085
Tell the client to keep the wound clean and dry.

00:01:05.582 --> 00:01:09.529
If over the next few days it becomes more swollen, red or painful,

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:11.005
they should see a doctor.

00:01:11.198 --> 00:01:13.085
Only then do you deal with the equipment.

00:01:13.264 --> 00:01:16.125
A surface with blood on it must always be disinfected.

00:01:16.474 --> 00:01:18.605
Those nippers do not go back into use;

00:01:18.822 --> 00:01:23.005
they go to be cleaned and sterilized, as in the lesson on tool processing.

00:01:23.418 --> 00:01:26.445
Disposable blades and needles go into a sharps container.

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:31.085
And if you keep pressing and the bleeding does not stop, call emergency services.

00:01:31.671 --> 00:01:32.204
Next:

00:01:32.353 --> 00:01:34.124
product splashing into the eye.

00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:37.724
Glue, tint, acetone, disinfectant.

00:01:38.233 --> 00:01:41.804
At that moment, the most important thing is to rinse immediately.

00:01:42.311 --> 00:01:47.731
Let clean water, lukewarm and not hot, run gently over the open eye, continuously,

00:01:47.681 --> 00:01:49.564
for at least twenty minutes.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.964
If the client wears contact lenses, ask them to take them out, if they can.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.284
Tell the client not to rub the eye.

00:01:56.631 --> 00:02:00.446
Then take the client to a doctor right away, and bring the product bottle,

00:02:00.396 --> 00:02:02.124
so the doctor can read the label.

00:02:02.385 --> 00:02:06.044
With strong chemicals, call emergency services while you keep rinsing.

00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:07.321
Next:

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:08.841
the client has a reaction.

00:02:09.096 --> 00:02:12.601
Itching, burning, redness, swelling.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.561
Stop, remove the product very gently, then rinse with plenty of water.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.881
I covered this in the lesson on allergies.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.521
Here I will only repeat the danger signs:

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:28.521
trouble breathing, a hoarse voice, swollen lips, a swollen face, dizziness.

00:02:28.949 --> 00:02:31.841
If you see these, call emergency services right away,

00:02:31.791 --> 00:02:34.041
and do not wait to see if it gets better.

00:02:34.221 --> 00:02:37.076
Ask whether the client carries an adrenaline auto injector,

00:02:37.026 --> 00:02:39.881
and help them into the position where breathing is easiest.

00:02:40.148 --> 00:02:42.921
Stay with the client, and do not leave them alone.

00:02:43.575 --> 00:02:44.931
Now, burns.

00:02:45.246 --> 00:02:46.611
Wax that is too hot.

00:02:46.798 --> 00:02:48.611
A nail that burns under the lamp.

00:02:48.865 --> 00:02:51.251
Bleach or perm solution burning the scalp.

00:02:51.506 --> 00:02:52.531
For heat burns:

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.851
cool it right away under cool running water.

00:02:55.151 --> 00:02:56.931
Current first aid guidance says:

00:02:57.193 --> 00:02:59.331
at least ten minutes, ideally twenty.

00:02:59.657 --> 00:03:02.931
Remove rings and bracelets near the burn, before it swells.

00:03:03.038 --> 00:03:03.731
No ice.

00:03:04.003 --> 00:03:06.771
No cream, no oil, no toothpaste.

00:03:07.039 --> 00:03:08.531
Do not pop blisters.

00:03:08.618 --> 00:03:11.651
Once it has cooled, cover it with clean cling film:

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.371
lay it on loosely, do not wrap it tight.

00:03:14.995 --> 00:03:16.389
When does it need a doctor?

00:03:16.873 --> 00:03:20.389
When the burn blisters, and is larger than the palm of their hand.

00:03:20.935 --> 00:03:21.909
When it is deep.

00:03:22.265 --> 00:03:24.709
When it is on the face, or over a joint.

00:03:25.091 --> 00:03:26.469
And every chemical burn.

00:03:26.974 --> 00:03:28.389
With chemicals on the skin:

00:03:28.653 --> 00:03:31.365
rinse with lots of water, for a long time,

00:03:31.315 --> 00:03:34.789
remove any towel or clothing soaked with the chemical,

00:03:34.899 --> 00:03:36.549
and do not put anything on it.

00:03:36.726 --> 00:03:40.949
And when a client says it feels hot under the lamp, take the hand out right away.

00:03:41.189 --> 00:03:45.669
It is a sign that the gel layer is too thick, or that the nail has become thin.

00:03:46.306 --> 00:03:47.529
Then there is fainting.

00:03:47.987 --> 00:03:49.637
It is common during waxing,

00:03:49.587 --> 00:03:53.369
when someone gets up too fast after lying down for a long time,

00:03:53.717 --> 00:03:55.369
or when a client is afraid of blood.

00:03:55.704 --> 00:03:59.929
The client says they feel dizzy, turns pale, breaks into a sweat:

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.729
lay them down right away, before they fall.

00:04:03.071 --> 00:04:04.169
Raise their legs.

00:04:04.258 --> 00:04:07.289
Loosen their collar, and open a window for fresh air.

00:04:07.784 --> 00:04:10.169
Usually within a minute, the client comes round.

00:04:10.431 --> 00:04:14.329
Let them rest lying down a little longer, then sit up very slowly.

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:19.186
But if the client does not come round within a minute, is not breathing normally,

00:04:19.136 --> 00:04:19.929
has a seizure,

00:04:20.118 --> 00:04:22.889
or has chest pain, call emergency services.

00:04:23.503 --> 00:04:24.573
One more incident:

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:29.053
when you yourself get pricked or cut by a tool that has been used on a client.

00:04:29.564 --> 00:04:32.333
Let the wound bleed gently under running water.

00:04:32.676 --> 00:04:35.693
Do not squeeze hard, and do not suck the wound.

00:04:36.029 --> 00:04:39.133
Wash with soap and plenty of water, then cover it.

00:04:39.638 --> 00:04:44.012
After that, tell the salon owner straight away, and contact a doctor,

00:04:43.962 --> 00:04:45.453
or occupational health,

00:04:45.642 --> 00:04:46.413
the same day.

00:04:46.751 --> 00:04:48.093
Do not shrug it off.

00:04:48.316 --> 00:04:50.220
Some diseases spread through blood,

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:53.133
and preventive treatment only works if it starts early.

00:04:53.799 --> 00:04:57.149
Once the first minute is over, there are the things that come after.

00:04:57.639 --> 00:04:58.269
First:

00:04:58.368 --> 00:04:59.709
be honest with the client.

00:04:59.967 --> 00:05:03.709
What happened, what you did, and what the client should watch for.

00:05:04.134 --> 00:05:08.349
Apologize sincerely, do not blame, and do not hide anything.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:09.389
Next:

00:05:09.578 --> 00:05:11.549
write an incident report the same day.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:17.330
Date and time, who did the service, what happened, which product, the batch number,

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.589
how you handled it,

00:05:18.778 --> 00:05:20.349
and what you advised the client.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:22.029
Then tell the salon owner.

00:05:22.378 --> 00:05:26.472
The owner checks whether the insurer, or any authority, must be informed,

00:05:26.422 --> 00:05:28.189
under the rules where you work.

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:29.865
And do not forget:

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.705
restock the first aid kit.

00:05:32.246 --> 00:05:37.425
The salon first aid kit should contain plasters in all sizes, sterile gauze,

00:05:37.375 --> 00:05:38.505
roller bandages,

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:43.292
medical tape, pads to cover the eyes, disposable gloves, scissors,

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.785
saline for rinsing eyes and wounds,

00:05:45.965 --> 00:05:47.625
and a first aid instruction sheet.

00:05:48.112 --> 00:05:49.785
Do not keep any medicines in it.

00:05:50.052 --> 00:05:53.305
Keep the kit where everyone knows to find it, and check it regularly:

00:05:53.536 --> 00:05:55.705
what has run out, and what has expired.

00:05:56.397 --> 00:05:57.324
One more thing:

00:05:57.653 --> 00:05:59.884
most incidents can be prevented in advance.

00:06:00.313 --> 00:06:03.884
Test the wax temperature on your own wrist before applying it to the client.

00:06:04.299 --> 00:06:07.964
Protect the eyes of the client carefully when using chemicals near the face.

00:06:08.381 --> 00:06:11.564
Do not rush, and do not look at your phone while you work.

00:06:11.754 --> 00:06:15.972
At the front desk, keep the emergency number and the salon address written down,

00:06:15.922 --> 00:06:18.524
so whoever calls can read them out straight away.

00:06:19.169 --> 00:06:21.335
You see, none of this is complicated.

00:06:21.444 --> 00:06:24.879
Stop, stay calm, do a few simple things correctly,

00:06:24.829 --> 00:06:27.655
and know when to call emergency services.

00:06:27.826 --> 00:06:28.535
Let me repeat:

00:06:28.884 --> 00:06:31.735
this lesson does not replace a first aid course.

00:06:31.844 --> 00:06:34.375
Take a course, and refresh it every few years.

00:06:34.641 --> 00:06:36.775
Rules also differ from country to country.

00:06:37.044 --> 00:06:39.655
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
